[Ebc459d1dffa94905abd1e4d2] 6.2.8.7. CUDA Graphs
6.2.8.7.
CUDA Graphs
CUDA Graphs present a new model for work submission in CUDA.
A graph is a series of operations, such as kernel launches, connected by dependencies, which is defined separately from its execution.
This allows a graph to be defined once and then launched repeatedly.

[E547ec0e63df45b23aaf14e8b] 6.2.8.7.1. Graph Structure
6.2.8.7.1. Graph Structure

An operation forms a node in a graph. The dependencies between the operations are the edges. These dependencies constrain the execution sequence of the operations.

An operation may be scheduled at any time once the nodes on which it depends are complete. Scheduling is left up to the CUDA system.

